sort: 14
id: DerErr007
error: <rule name> must be the last justification on a line
text: You appear to be queuing a sequence of justifications on a single line.  However, since you may only Box and Cancel in the last line of a subderivation, the justification <rule name> must always be the last rule in such a queue .

sort: 15
id: DerErr008
error: <rule name> must be on the last line of a subderivation
text: You appear to be attempting to Box and Cancel on a line that has other lines from the same subderivation below it. You may Box and Cancel only in the bottom line of a subderivation. This subderivation contains <branch lines left> below the present line.\n\nYou may wish to delete <branch lines left> or the present line using the Alt+Delete key combination. \n\nTo recreate the present line at the bottom of the subderivation, add a new, empty line as follows: First verify that that the subderivation is not already boxed. If it is, Unbox using Ctrl+Shift+X. Then place the cursor in the present bottom line of the subderivation, and press Alt+Enter. (In Command Mode, Alt+Enter produces a new line without executing any command.)

sort: 16
id: DerErr009
error: <rule name> cannot be last on box and cancel line
text: You appear to be queuing a sequence of justifications on a single line.  However, since you are attempting to justify a Box and Cancel step, the justification for that action (DD, CD, ID, or UD) must always be the last rule in such a queue.

