sort: 52
id: DerErr045
error: line <remote line number> contains an uncanceled "Show"
text: You appear to have cited a Show line to which the present line is subordinate.  A Show line cannot be cited to justify a subordinate line.  \n\nOrdinarily, such a Show line would contain an uncanceled Show until the present line is boxed.  Such lines cannot be used until the Show is canceled.
description: This is raised when the line cited is a Show line in whose derivation the current line resides

sort: 53
id: DerErr046
error: line <remote line number> is already boxed (or should be)
text: You appear to be attempting to use a line that is not "antecedent" to the present line.  Lines that are already boxed may not be used to justify succeeding steps.\n\nLine <remote line number> lies within a subderivation that either is boxed or should have been boxed before the present line was entered. \n\nTo determine the Show line to which line <line number> is subordinate, place your cursor in line <line number>, and note the "Show" that appears in reverse highlight.
description: This message is sent when the cited line is in a box (or *should* be in a box) within another subderivation.

