sort: 68
id: DerErr061
error: improper substitution
text: It appears that you are attempting to apply the rule <rule name>.  However, the substitution you propose will cause a clash of variables.  \n\nEither, there is a free occurrence of <arg 1> in <stack 1> which would be picked up by the quantifier phrase <operator><arg 1>, or <stack 1> already contains an internal quantifier on <arg 1> that will capture the new occurrences of <arg 1>.  \n\nIn answer to the request to specify a variable of generalization, you must specify a variable that is not free in <stack 1>, and that will not be captured by an existing quantifier in <stack 1>.
description: EG that either picks up a wrong variable or in which the generalized variable gets picked up by an internal quantifier.

sort: 69
id: DerErr062
